              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dispōnō, dispōnere — \"to set out, to arrange\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mīlitēs in mūrīs dispositī sunt. The soldiers were posted along the walls."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dispōnō, dispōnere, disposuī, dispositum: dis- + pōnō, to place here and there. English dispose."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dispōnō is built from dis- \"apart\" and pōnō \"to put\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): to put each thing in its own place. English dispose comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
