              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mōlior, mōlīrī — \"to set about (with effort), to undertake; to plot\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Magnam rem mōlītur. He is setting about a great undertaking."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Deponent: mōlior, mōlīrī, mōlītus sum, built on mōlēs, a mass: to heave a heavy thing. English demolish comes from dēmōlior, to pull down."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mōlior is built on mōlēs \"a mass, a heavy weight\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): to move a great weight. English demolish comes from its compound dēmōlior."
            }
          ]
        },
